<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Cloud backup contents on API 23-30 (dataExtractionRules covers 31+).

  Include-only, deliberately. Intention is a self-blocking app, so its own
  state is exactly what a determined user would restore to defeat it: an
  edited intention_prefs.xml puts back an empty blocklist, or an activeSessions
  entry with a huge intervalMinutes. Nothing about blocking is backed up.

  intention_billing is the exception and must stay included. It holds the
  account UUID that keys the coaching-credit balance server-side (see
  BillingManager.stableAccountId and server/src/app.js's subjectFor). Credits
  are consumables, consumed immediately, so Play cannot re-report them — lose that UUID and the paid balance is orphaned with no recovery path.
  Restoring a chosen UUID is not a blocking bypass, and taking someone else's
  balance would mean guessing a v4 UUID.

  Include-only also fails safe: anything added later (a new prefs file, WebView
  local storage, a database) is excluded until someone deliberately lists it.
-->
<full-backup-content>
    <include domain="sharedpref" path="intention_billing.xml" />
</full-backup-content>
